# L §6.5 change 3 (a retroactive law change), copied whole in the round-7 text: its two moves bind `a in adjustments
# on act_day`, act_day = 2028-06-15 a row (L §7.1), so they bind the adjustments dated 2028-06-15.
# adv: the 24 advance adjustments (twelve per taxpayer) sum to 24 * -30.00 = -720.00 PLN; set: the two
# settlements' to -1 440.00 PLN (L §5.14.3 `sum(a.change for a in adjustments ...)`).
# booked: "A booked amount never changes afterwards" (E §5 step 6): 5 400.00 and 450.00 PLN.
# ref: refund_2027 refunds -a.change = 720.00 PLN per taxpayer on 2029-04-30: flows of the move 1 440.00 PLN
# (L §5.14.3 flows(m, span)); fisc's flows in the late half of June 2028 are the two June advances, 900.00 PLN, no
# hole: the advances' adjustments are waived and the settlements' are fulfilled (E §5 step 5).  Every plan instance
# before the cut that a sum counts and no observation fulfils is listed `unfulfilled:` (L §8.2).
# old: L §6.5 says "ask ... as known 2028-06-14 still shows the old view". At that cut act_day has no row (its
# only row is in pit_2027_refund, known 2028-06-15), so the moves' bindings `a in adjustments on act_day where
# a.adjusts in ...` have a hole day; L §5.7 Bindings (round 8): such a binding is a hole only where a thing of the
# kind, known at the cut, could be alive on one of its possible days, and binds nothing where none could. The only
# adjustments known at that cut are the base's wage adjustments, which the binding's where rules out whatever the
# day, so it binds nothing: refund_2027 has no instance and its flows are 0.00 PLN, the old view. (Was
# REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED §4.6, the HOLE-UNGOVERNED question with no law date.)
# The base excerpt (L §6.5) copied whole, with a header (on 2028-07-01, after the change's known date, §6.2 advance),
# and the items change 3 names that the excerpt doesn't show, declared minimally: "The base's moves pit_advance
# (monthly, of kind pit_advances) and pit_settle (the annual return, of kind pit_settlements, paid from the
# taxpayer's account to fisc) aren't shown above."  pit_advance pays round(pit[p, year] / 24) on day 20 of each
# month; pit_settle pays, on 30 April of the next year, pit[p, y] less the advances as booked ("the settlement,
# which reads the advances as booked").  taxable = income - pit_free (income 120 000.00 PLN, pit_free 30 000.00 PLN
# in a completion version), read `at start_of(y)` as the base's pit is (round 7).
# Hand-checked from the stated rules: 2027 tax 12 % * 90 000 = 10 800 PLN, advances 450.00 PLN, settlement
# 10 800 - 12 * 450 = 5 400.00 PLN.  Under change 3, tax 12 % * 84 000 = 10 080 PLN: each 2027 advance changes by
# 420.00 - 450.00 = -30.00 PLN, each settlement by 10 080 - 5 400 - 5 400 = -720.00 PLN (E §5 step 3), all dated
# 2028-06-15 (step 4).
# (Writer 8: L §5.10 refuses a unit stated on an outside place, and flows of a place of unit any is refused (L §5.14.3),
# so fisc is a thing of its own outside kind of unit PLN, tax_offices.)
=== change3.tally
part change3
  tally 2

source pit_2027_retro "Ustawa z 2028-06-15, art. 2: stosuje się od 2027-01-01"

kind waivers: event certain
input refund_day: date
input act_day: date

version pit_2027_refund
  cite pit_2027_retro
  governs 2027
  known 2028-06-15
  replace pit_free = 36 000.00 PLN "art. 2 ust. 1"
  refund_day = 2029-04-30 governs always "art. 2 ust. 2"
  act_day = 2028-06-15 governs always "tytuł ustawy"

move keep_advances[a in adjustments on act_day where a.adjusts in pit_advances]: waivers
  on a.day
  fulfils a

move refund_2027[a in adjustments on act_day where a.adjusts in pit_settlements]: transfers
  on refund_day
  leg cash from fisc to a.adjusts.cash.from amount -a.change
  fulfils a

ask adv: sum(a.change for a in adjustments over 2028-06-15 where a.adjusts in pit_advances)
ask set: sum(a.change for a in adjustments over 2028-06-15 where a.adjusts in pit_settlements)
ask booked: pit_settle[2027, ana].cash.amount, pit_advance[2027-03, ana].cash.amount
ask ref: flows(refund_2027, 2029), flows(fisc, 2028-06-15 .. 2028-06-30)
ask old: flows(refund_2027, 2029) as known 2028-06-14
=== household.tally
model household
  tally 2
  on 2028-07-01
  start 2026-10-01
  end 2030-12-31

source household "the household's own records"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
index instalments = [equal, decreasing]
index overpay_choices = [shorter, lower]
index pit_brackets = [low, high]
index countries = [pl, de]
index tax_years = year 2026..2040

kind persons
kind jobs
kind loans
kind wages: event certain
  leg cash: PLN

place konto[p in persons]: accounts PLN lives 2019-05-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..

input loan_terms[l in loans]: (principal money PLN, months int, plan key instalments)
input overpay[l in loans, m in months]: (amount money PLN, choice key overpay_choices)
input parent[c in persons, k in persons]: bool
input pay_dom[j in jobs]: int
input pit_free: money PLN
input pit_rate[b in pit_brackets]: num
input residence[p in persons, m in months]: key countries
input salary[j in jobs, m in months]: money PLN question "Ile wynosi pensja brutto z tej pracy w tym miesiącu?"
input works_for[j in jobs]: key persons

band pit_scale(x: num PLN): num PLN
def net_wage[j in jobs, m in months]: money PLN = salary[j, m] at start_of(m)
def taxable[p in persons, y in tax_years]: money PLN = max(income - pit_free, 0 PLN) at start_of(y)

def pit[p in persons, y in tax_years]: money PLN at start_of(y)
  rule base = round(pit_scale(taxable[p, y]), 1 PLN, half-up)
  rule abroad beats base = ?"Podatek nierezydenta Polski nie jest opisany." when residence[p, month_of(start_of(y))] != pl

move wage[m in months, j in jobs over m]: wages
  on day_of(m, pay_dom[j])
  at start_of(m)
  leg cash from world to konto[works_for[j]] amount net_wage[j, m]

version home_2026
  cite household
  governs 2026-10..
  known 2026-10-19
  persons + [ana] lives 1990-04-02..
  persons + [ben] lives 1988-11-30..
  jobs + [ana_acme] lives 2020-02-01..
  jobs + [ben_bolt] lives 2021-09-01..
  parent = false "brak dzieci"
  pay_dom = 10 "umowy o pracę, § 5"
  residence = pl "meldunek w Krakowie"
  works_for[ana_acme] = ana
  works_for[ben_bolt] = ben
  opening[konto[ana]] = 12 400.00 PLN at 2026-10-01 start "wyciąg"
  opening[konto[ben]] = 3 150.00 PLN at 2026-10-01 start "wyciąg"
  pit_scale: [0, inf) = 12 % * x "art. 27"

kind pit_advances: event certain
  leg cash: PLN
kind pit_settlements: event certain
  leg cash: PLN
kind tax_offices: place PLN signed outside
place fisc: tax_offices lives 1900-01-01..
input income: money PLN
input adv_dom: int
input adv_parts: int
input settle_lag: int
input settle_dom: int

move pit_advance[m in months, p in persons on day_of(m, adv_dom)]: pit_advances
  on day_of(m, adv_dom)
  at start_of(m)
  leg cash from konto[p] to fisc amount round(pit[p, year_of(start_of(m))] / adv_parts, minor(PLN), half-up)

move pit_settle[y in tax_years, p in persons on day_of(month_of(add_months(end_of(y), settle_lag)), settle_dom)]: pit_settlements
  on day_of(month_of(add_months(end_of(y), settle_lag)), settle_dom)
  at end_of(y)
  leg cash from konto[p] to fisc amount pit[p, y] - sum(a.cash.amount for a in pit_advances over y where a.cash.from == konto[p])

version base_figures
  cite household
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-10-01
  income = 120 000.00 PLN "PIT-11"
  pit_free = 30 000.00 PLN "art. 27"
  adv_dom = 20 "art. 44"
  adv_parts = 24 "art. 44"
  settle_lag = 3 "art. 45"
  settle_dom = 30 "art. 45"
